 1 "// readyTypes completes every registered type once, after every file's init has set its slots"] [171 1 "// (CPython's PyType_Ready): bases, MRO, and the slots a type leaves nil inherited from its base."] [189 2 "// type_ready's type_dict_set_doc: a static type's dict always holds __doc__, its tp_doc or None (pyi has no C"] [190 2 "// docstrings yet: None), so an instance's __doc__ is found (\"abc\".__doc__ raised AttributeError; email's"] [191 2 "// _policybase reads attr.__doc__ of every class attribute); not where the type or a base answers __doc__ by a"] [192 2 "// getset (pyi's getsets are outside the dict: property's settable __doc__ would be shadowed)"] [200 1 "// docGetSet reports whether a type of t's MRO has a __doc__ getset."] [223 1 "// inheritSlots fills s's nil slots from b's (CPython's inherit_slots)."] [322 1 "// ownSlots are the special methods a built-in type defines itself, before inheritSlots fills the rest:"] [323 1 "// its __dict__ lists their slot wrappers, as CPython's does (enum's _find_data_type_ asks"] [324 1 "// '__new__' in int.__dict__). Added by PY5e as the integration's owner (part 2b)."] [341 2 "// add_operators: the number protocol's and the comparisons' wrappers (PY6e's REQUEST d27906db)"] [366 1 "// slottedName: the special methods recordOwnSlots records; ownsSlot is built-in type m showing name's wrapper in"] [367 1 "// its own __dict__: a subclass inherits the slot, so that bool.__add__ is int.__add__ as in CPython."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[38 40]] :go/trails [[138 122]]} (go/file "registry.go" :imports [])

;; The registry of built-in types and functions (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.3): each file of the runtime
;; declares its types as package variables made by NewBuiltinType (no slots: slots are set in the file's
;; init function, after every type exists, so the slots' functions may name any type) and registers
;; its built-in functions with RegisterBuiltin. The builtins module of an Interp is made from the
;; registry: every registered type and function whose name is public, in registration order.

